e] with value [this] and unit `\"pib\"` (pebibytes).\n\nFacts:\n```\n1.pib == 1024.tib\n```"; annotations = List(); modifiers = Set("abstract"); name = "pib"; allModifiers = Set("abstract"); allAnnotations = List() }, "sign", new Property { location { line = 851; column = 3; displayUri = "https://github.com/apple/pkl/blob/0.32.0/stdlib/base.pkl#L851" }; docComment = "The sign of this number.\n\nReturns `0` for `0`, `0.0`, `-0.0`, and [NaN],\n`1` for positive numbers (including [Infinity]),\nand `-1` for negative numbers (including `-`[Infinity])."; annotations = List(); modifiers = Set("abstract"); name = "sign"; allModifiers = Set("abstract"); allAnnotations = List() }, "abs", new Property { location { line = 865; column = 3; displayUri = "https://github.com/apple/pkl/blob/0.32.0/stdlib/base.pkl#L865" }; docComment = "The absolute value of this number.\n\nFacts:\n```\n42.abs == 42\n-42.abs == 42\n0.0.abs == 0.0\n(-0.0).abs == 0.0\nInfinity.abs == Infinity\n(-Infinity).abs == Infinity\nNaN.abs == NaN\n```"; annotations = List(); modifiers = Set("abstract"); name = "abs"; allModifiers = Set("abstract"); allAnnotations = List() }, "ceil", new Property { location { line = 873; column = 3; displayUri = "https://github.com/apple/pkl/blob/0.32.0/stdlib/base.pkl#L873" }; docComment = "Rounds this number to the next mathematical integer towards [Infinity].\n\nIf [this] is an [Int], returns [this].\nIf [this] is [NaN], [Infinity], -[Infinity], `0.0`, or `-0.0`, returns [this].\nOtherwise, returns the smallest [Float] that is greater than or equal to [this]\nand is equal to a mathematical integer."; annotations = List(); modifiers = Set("abstract"); name = "ceil"; allModifiers = Set("abstract"); allAnnotations = List() }, "floor", new Property { location { line = 881; column = 3; displayUri = "https://github.com/apple/pkl/blob/0.32.0/stdlib/base.pkl#L881" }; docComment = "Rounds this number to the next mathematical integer towards -[Infinity].\n\nIf [this] is an [Int], return